{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ropeable-celestine-ragfish","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThere is a latent 4-hop import cycle in `src/rebar/llm/`, held open only by two deferred\n(function-body) imports:\n\n1. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py:38` — `from rebar.llm.completion import\n   verify_step_floor` — **module level**\n2. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:43` — `from . import completion_banking as\n   _bank` — **module level**\n3. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:684` — `from .completion_recovery import\n   CompletionAgentStep, raise_completion_workflow_failure` — **inside a function**\n   (`_produce_completion_verdict_dispatch`)\n4. `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:446` — `from rebar.llm.workflow import gate_dispatch` —\n   **inside a function** (`verify_completion`)\n\n`verify_step_floor` (defined `completion.py:235`) is a ~15-line pure arithmetic clamp\n(criteria count + direct-child count + `VerifyConfig` fields -> an integer step floor). It is\nthe *only* reason `completion_banking.py` needs a module-level edge back into `completion.py`.\nBoth deferred imports are currently unmarked as cycle-breakers — an agent who tidies up either\nlazy import (a very ordinary refactor move) silently breaks the package import at runtime. That\ninvisibility, not the cycle itself, is the complexity cost: nothing in the tree flags these two\nimports as load-bearing.\n\n**Verified by execution on `origin/main@2e28d817a7eefca3935a0ead4c84d584eda8c201`** (not by\nreading): copied `src/` to a scratch directory, used an `ast`-based hoist (parses the module to\nfind the true end-of-import-block line, so the inserted statement can never land inside a\nparenthesized import or before the module docstring) to move imports 3 and 4 to module level,\nthen imported:\n\n```\nImportError: cannot import name 'verify_step_floor' from partially initialized module\n'rebar.llm.completion' (most likely due to a circular import)\n  .../rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py, line 43, in <module>\n      from . import completion_banking as _bank\n  .../rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py, line ~38 (post-hoist), in <module>\n      from rebar.llm.completion import verify_step_floor\n```\n\nHoisting import 4 alone (without import 3) imports cleanly — confirming import 4 alone does not\nclose the loop; both edges hoisted together is what reproduces the cycle.\n\n## Approach\n\nMove `verify_step_floor` and its private constant `_VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX` (`completion.py:67`)\nout of `completion.py` into `src/rebar/llm/config.py`. `config.py` is the semantically correct\nhome: `verify_step_floor`'s only non-literal input is `verify_cfg` (a `VerifyConfig` instance;\nthe function reads `completion_verify_steps_per_criterion`, `completion_verify_step_floor_min`,\n`completion_verify_child_traversal_steps`, `completion_verify_fixed_overhead_steps` off it), so\nthe clamp is a config-driven computation, not a completion-verification behavior. `config.py`\ndoes not import `completion.py` (directly or transitively — confirmed by reading its import\nblock), so moving the function there cannot recreate the cycle, and it is already the\nestablished home for config-adjacent helpers like `available_backends()`. `config.py` is 553\nLOC and the move adds ~23 LOC (code + the existing comment), landing it at ~576 LOC — well under\nthe 800 LOC hard cap, though above the 200–500 target band (noted, not blocking: splitting\n`config.py` is out of scope for this ticket).\n\nAfter the move, `completion.py` re-imports `verify_step_floor` from `rebar.llm.config` at\nmodule level (`completion.py` already imports `VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL, LLMConfig` from\n`rebar.llm.config`, so this adds one name to an existing import, not a new edge) so its own call\nsite (`completion.py:433`) keeps working, and so `completion.verify_step_floor` remains a\nresolvable module attribute for the existing `monkeypatch.setattr(completion, \"verify_step_floor\",\n...)` test seam (see Testing). `completion_banking.py:38` is re-pointed to import the function\nfrom `rebar.llm.config` instead of `rebar.llm.completion`. With `completion_banking.py` no\nlonger needing a module-level edge into `completion.py`, imports 3 and 4 can both become\nordinary module-level imports (hoisted to the top of `gate_dispatch.py` and `completion.py`\nrespectively) with no remaining edge to close the loop.\n\n**Verified by execution:** applied this exact move in the scratch copy, re-hoisted both edges,\nand `import rebar.llm.completion, rebar.llm.workflow.gate_dispatch, rebar.llm` succeeded\ncleanly. A whole-tree `pkgutil.walk_packages` sweep over `rebar.*` (using the project's venv)\nfound exactly the same 2 pre-existing, unrelated failures as the unmodified tree\n(`rebar.opcert_service.app` and `rebar.review_bot.app`, both `ModuleNotFoundError: No module\nnamed 'fastapi'` — `fastapi` is simply not installed in this venv). No new failure, no new\ncycle.\n\nThis is scoped to moving **one function** and closing **one cycle** — it explicitly does NOT\nhoist the ~258 other lazy imports across `llm/`. That broader move was proposed and separately\ntested by a prior review: hoisting lazy imports generally binds the imported name into the\nimporting module's namespace at load time, so a later `monkeypatch.setattr` targeting the\n*original* source module (an extremely common test pattern in this suite — the majority of the\n~2,900 patch call sites in the suite are this object-form, not the string-form\n`importlib`/`\"pkg.mod.name\"` form) no longer reaches the call site, producing silent false\npasses or spurious failures. That broad proposal produced 4 regression files / 6 failing tests\nwhen tested and was refuted on those grounds. This ticket touches exactly the two edges whose\ncycle was reproduced by execution above, and preserves every existing patch seam by verifying\neach one individually (see Testing).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/completion.py` — remove `verify_step_floor` (`:235`) and `_VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX`\n  (`:67`); add `verify_step_floor` to the existing `from rebar.llm.config import ...` line;\n  hoist the `from rebar.llm.workflow import gate_dispatch` import (currently inside\n  `verify_completion`, `:446`) to module level.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — add `verify_step_floor` and `_VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX` (moved\n  verbatim, including the existing docstring/comment).\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py` — re-point the `:38` import from\n  `rebar.llm.completion` to `rebar.llm.config`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` — hoist the `from .completion_recovery import\n  CompletionAgentStep, raise_completion_workflow_failure` import (currently inside\n  `_produce_completion_verdict_dispatch`, `:684`) to module level.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_completion_budget.py` — re-point the `:20` import\n  (`from rebar.llm.completion import _VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX, verify_step_floor` ->\n  `from rebar.llm.config import ...`).\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_verdict_cache.py` — re-point the `:549` in-test import\n  (`from rebar.llm.completion import verify_step_floor` -> `from rebar.llm.config import\n  verify_step_floor`).\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_wrapper_duration_instrumentation.py` — no code change expected\n  at `:455` (`monkeypatch.setattr(completion, \"verify_step_floor\", step_floor)` keeps working\n  because `completion.py` still exposes `verify_step_floor` as a module attribute via the\n  re-import); verify by running the test, not by inspection alone.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Run the 3 directly affected test files (`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_completion_budget.py`,\n  `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_verdict_cache.py`,\n  `tests/unit/test_completion_wrapper_duration_instrumentation.py`) and confirm all pass —\n  these are the exhaustive set of non-source references to the moved symbols (confirmed by\n  `grep -rn \"verify_step_floor\\|_VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX\" src tests docs`).\n- Confirm `python -c \"import rebar.llm.completion, rebar.llm.workflow.gate_dispatch, rebar.llm\"`\n  succeeds with both lazy imports hoisted to module level (the state the fix leaves the tree\n  in) — this is the regression check for the cycle this ticket closes.\n- Run `make verify` (lint + typecheck + import-convention guard + the full `not integration and\n  not external` suite) and confirm it passes — this is the project's CI-equivalent contract and\n  covers the whole-tree AST/cycle-adjacent scans that a narrower run would miss.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `verify_step_floor` and `_VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX` are defined in `src/rebar/llm/config.py`\n      and no longer in `src/rebar/llm/completion.py`; checked by `grep -n \"def verify_step_floor\"\n      src/rebar/llm/config.py` (1 hit) and the same grep against `completion.py` (0 hits).\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:684`'s `from .completion_recovery import\n      CompletionAgentStep, raise_completion_workflow_failure` and\n      `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:446`'s `from rebar.llm.workflow import gate_dispatch` are\n      both module-level imports (no longer inside a function body); checked by reading the\n      diff and confirming neither import line is indented.\n- [ ] `python -c \"import rebar.llm.completion, rebar.llm.workflow.gate_dispatch, rebar.llm\"`\n      exits 0 from the worktree root with the venv active.\n- [ ] The 3 affected test files (`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_completion_budget.py`,\n      `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_verdict_cache.py`,\n      `tests/unit/test_completion_wrapper_duration_instrumentation.py`) pass under\n      `python -m pytest` run with the bare `pytest` console script.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes (lint, typecheck, import-convention guard, full `not integration and\n      not external` suite) — the project's CI-equivalent contract.\n- [ ] No file in `src/rebar` exceeds 800 LOC after the change (checked by `wc -l\n      src/rebar/llm/config.py src/rebar/llm/completion.py`; `config.py` is expected to land\n      near 576 LOC, `completion.py` near 452 LOC — both well under the cap).\n","id":"8246-a1f4-2cf1-4a22","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Move verify_step_floor out of completion.py to close a latent 4-hop import cycle in llm/"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793821764268861372,"uuid":"a2d55a28-47a7-4b02-a496-5e73e3a469d5"}